yarn-error.log*

# Tailwind CSS output is deliberately NOT ignored. It is a committed artifact:
# node_modules is not in the repo, so a fresh clone has no way to generate it and
# the app would render unstyled without it. The file was already tracked despite
# the old ignore rule here — force-added at some point — which meant the rule did
# nothing except mislead anyone who deleted the file and tried to add it back.

# Package lock files (optional - some teams commit these)
package-lock.json

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local 
# Generated at build time from Microsoft.AspNetCore.App.Internal.Assets; see the
# CopyBlazorWebScript target in DevToolbox.UI.csproj.
DevToolbox.UI/wwwroot/_framework/

# Regenerated by the SDK whenever a web project is run, with a random applicationUrl
# each time. Nothing reads it: WebPreviewHost binds the port itself, which is what the
# "Overriding address(es)" warning on startup is. Tracking it would mean a spurious diff
# for whoever ran the app last.
**/Properties/launchSettings.json